<title>NETHERLANDS: ABN AMRO increases &quot;Nifty 15&quot; warrants issue.</title>
<headline>ABN AMRO increases &quot;Nifty 15&quot; warrants issue.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABN AMRO said it had increased the number of American-style call warrants it had issued on a basket of shares of 15 Dutch companies known as the &quot;Nifty Fifteen&quot; to 1.5 million from an original one million.</p>
<p>One basket is controlled by 100 warrants. The warrants are exercisable until December 4, 1998 and the strike price is 11,799 guilders.</p>
<p>The basket is made up of Aegon, Ahold, Baan, CSM, Elsevier, Getronics, Hagemeyer, Heineken, IHC Caland, Nutricia, Oce, Polygram, Randstad, VNU, Wolters Kluwer.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
